        </AlertDescription>
      </Alert>
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the policy to RHACM by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f pause-<mcp_name>-policy.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Include the pause policy in your <code>ClusterGroupUpgrade</code> custom resource (CR) before the update policy:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: ran.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: ClusterGroupUpgrade\nmetadata:\n  name: <cgu_name>\n  namespace: <namespace>\nspec:\n  clusters:\n  - <cluster_name>\n  managedPolicies:\n  - pause-<mcp_name>\n  - <upgrade_policy_name>\n  enable: false\n  remediationStrategy:\n    maxConcurrency: 1\n    timeout: 120"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>TALM applies the pause policy before applying the update policy, ensuring workers remain paused during the control plane update.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      After the control plane update completes and you are ready to update worker nodes, create an unpause policy for each <code>MachineConfigPool</code> resource:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1\nkind: Policy\nmetadata:\n  name: unpause-<mcp_name>\n  namespace: openshift-upgrade-policies\nspec:\n  disabled: false\n  policy-templates:\n    - objectDefinition:\n        apiVersion: policy.open-cluster-management.io/v1\n        evaluationInterval:\n          compliant: never\n        kind: ConfigurationPolicy\n        metadata:\n          name: unpause-<mcp_name>\n        spec:\n          object-templates:\n            - complianceType: musthave\n              objectDefinition:\n                apiVersion: machineconfiguration.openshift.io/v1\n                kind: MachineConfigPool\n                metadata:\n                  name: <mcp_name>\n                spec:\n                  paused: false\n          remediationAction: inform\n          severity: low\n  remediationAction: inform"} lang="yaml" />
      <p>where <code>&lt;mcp_name&gt;</code> is the name of the machine config pool to unpause, for example <code>mcp-1</code>.</p>
      <p>The unpause policies for each machine config pool are included as managed policies in the final <code>ClusterGroupUpgrade</code> CR. When TALM enforces these policies, the machine config pools unpause and all accumulated configuration changes are applied in a single reboot per node.</p>
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the unpause policy by using a <code>ClusterGroupUpgrade</code> CR:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: ran.openshift.io/v1alpha1\nkind: ClusterGroupUpgrade\nmetadata:\n  name: <cgu_name>\n  namespace: <namespace>\nspec:\n  clusters:\n  - <cluster_name>\n  managedPolicies:\n  - unpause-<mcp_name>\n  enable: false\n  remediationStrategy:\n    maxConcurrency: 1"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply and enable the <code>ClusterGroupUpgrade</code> CR to unpause workers by running the following commands:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f <unpause_cgu_cr_filename>.yaml\n$ oc patch cgu <cgu_name> \\\n  -n <namespace> \\\n  --type merge \\\n  -p '{\"spec\":{\"enable\":true}}'"} lang="terminal" />
