      <h2 id="core-cluster-upgrade-worker-node-management-manual_core-cluster-upgrades-worker-management" class="group scroll-mt-20">Pausing and unpausing worker nodes by using machine config pools<a href="#core-cluster-upgrade-worker-node-management-manual_core-cluster-upgrades-worker-management" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">You can pause and unpause worker nodes directly by patching the <code>MachineConfigPool</code> resource on the target cluster. Use this method when you are managing a single cluster or when you do not have Topology Aware Lifecycle Manager (TALM) configured.</p>
